# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for OxwaldEngine.
#
# Usage (from the repo root):
#   TSAN_OPTIONS="suppressions=$PWD/tools/sanitizers/tsan.supp" ./build/<tsan-dir>/bin/ox_core_tests
#
# Currently no suppressions are needed. enkiTS (ox::JobSystem's backend) is a prebuilt,
# NON-instrumented vcpkg library, so the happens-before edges it creates (lock-free task pipes,
# m_RunningCount acquire/release, semaphores) are invisible to TSan. engine/core/src/jobs.cpp
# mirrors them with __tsan_release/__tsan_acquire annotations (compiled only under TSan): submit ->
# ExecuteRange/Forward::Execute -> completion (done()/wait()/waitAll()/shutdown). Without those
# annotations every job hand-off was reported as a (false-positive) race.
#
# This file is kept so scripts that reference it keep working. The former blanket suppressions are
# left commented out for reference; do not re-enable them, as they also hide real races between job
# bodies. If a new enkiTS-internal report appears, add a narrowly scoped line with an explanation.
#race:enki::TaskScheduler::TryRunTask
#race:enki::TaskScheduler::RunPinnedTasks
